dded the daily fee to the number of days instead of multiplying. It now multiplies.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned `n+1` events. It now returns the last `n`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the policy comment and the tests say 5. I set it to 5.\n\u001b[0m\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +1ms service=session session=ses_e9b1396b9ffeg0shS4N1lAMGXl type=finish-step part\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +1ms service=bus type=message.part.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +1ms service=session session=ses_e9b1396b9ffeg0shS4N1lAMGXl type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +3ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +0ms service=session session=ses_e9b1396b9ffeg0shS4N1lAMGXl sessionID=ses_e9b1396b9ffeg0shS4N1lAMGXl unlocking\n`python3 -m unittest` now passes: all 16 tests run and report OK. I didn't touch the tests. The fixes in `catalog/`:\n\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` left the year as a string. It now converts it to an int.\n- **`factory.py`**: `sample_books()` was missing Emma, so I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The author, year and copy count are my choice. The tests only check the title.\n- **`fees.py`**: `late_fee` added the daily fee to the number of days instead of multiplying. It now multiplies.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned `n+1` events. It now returns the last `n`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the policy comment and the tests say 5. I set it to 5.INFO  2026-10-22T18:43:12 +2ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_req